abstract: >-
  An independent audit of CyberChainBench (arXiv:2606.26216) against its own
  public release at commit 1cb7410. The patch subset (94 cases), the patch
  arithmetic (23.4% = 22/94) and the temporal split reproduce; the 200-case
  exploit set behind 43.7% is not published. The paper reports three
  different best patch scores, its Tables 4 and 5 disagree for one
  configuration, and the leaderboard shipped with the release differs from
  Table 4 for 6 of 10 configurations. Read from code, the patch oracle tests
  byte equality of replayed calls, counts any change as blocking and
  out-of-gas as preserved, and has no reported calibration. No model or
  chain was run.
